(text "ENA (pin 1) and ENB (pin 9) take PWM for speed.\nIN1/IN2 set M1's direction, IN3/IN4 set M2's:\n  HIGH/LOW = forward, LOW/HIGH = back, equal = brake." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 154.94 134.62 0)
  (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1e9cc200-acd5-5c97-a2c1-dc0701b06b7a"))
(text "VCC1 = 5 V logic from the UNO. VCC2 = separate motor supply (4.5 V to 36 V).\nThe L293D drops about 2.6 V (1.4 V high side + 1.2 V low side), so 9 V\nleaves roughly 6 V across a motor. Limit: 600 mA per channel.\nIts built-in clamp diodes are the flyback diodes. Grounds are shared." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 162.56 40.64 0)
  (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "09fa1bc8-3818-59b3-b804-e5912a3dd036"))
(text "A5 Question 3: two motors on an L293D\nDesign only, not built" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 50.8 40.64 0)
  (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cb272b91-a29a-57b7-a88e-d76b469d4e12"))
